cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Emotion vectors in Gemma-4-31B: circumplex replication, what instruction tuning displaces, and tracking emotion through a story"
abstract: >-
  A replication of Sofroniew et al. (2026), "Emotion Concepts and their Function
  in a Large Language Model", which found internal representations of emotion
  concepts in Claude Sonnet 4.5 that causally influence the model's outputs. This
  work tests whether the finding transfers to an open-weights model, Gemma-4-31B:
  difference-of-means emotion vectors from the residual stream, a valence-arousal
  circumplex geometry check, and the cosine-similarity control-prompt validation
  that the earlier open replication omitted. The base checkpoint reproduces the
  circumplex; the instruction-tuned checkpoint does not, and one large
  non-affective direction dominates it instead. A second line of work, not in the
  original paper, reads emotion vectors token by token through stories written to
  move between three emotions, and finds tracking above chance but uneven, with a
  large share of the variation attributable to who wrote the stories the vectors
  were built from.
type: software
authors:
